  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_0d1a1dc8b5c94c78ac9ec66694ea13c5",
      "statement": "The stylesheet override exists because widening the content column requires passing `$main-content-max-width` to the theme's variables module at `@use` time, which means owning a copy of the theme's Sass entrypoint.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://assets/css/jekyll-theme-chirpy.scss#L1-L15",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d1daffaf6bc35a4e644d9d1e10ef703a04e4211071b3d103b082585a2084ad77:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b55de216db404251924d059bd55c5998",
      "statement": "Widening content to 1600px pushes Chirpy's back-to-top `calc()` position negative between the 1650px breakpoint and roughly 1900px of viewport, so the override floors it with an interpolated CSS `max()` that Sass emits rather than evaluates.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://assets/css/jekyll-theme-chirpy.scss#L71-L82",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e0719b9c313e92248d71a2930347784c0824de5844943fb391ffcf1acfa4fe97:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_01425698643d4a3baf710d78aeec8a2c",
      "statement": "The post layout override is a verbatim copy of the gem's layout whose only intentional difference is adding `newsletter` to the front of `tail_includes`, making it the highest-risk override because upstream changes to that layout are silently frozen at the copied version.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://THEME_UPGRADE.md#L48-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cb530f3f93bb7e851622aa3ee80785aa632af55b513d6a5bcced856d7f3eb3bd:"
